# Copy to `.env.production` and fill in with your own Firebase project's
# values (from the Firebase console: Project settings > General > Your apps
# > SDK setup and configuration) once cross-device sync is ready to go live -
# or just run scripts/setup_firebase.py, which writes this file for you.
# See docs/adr/0006 for what these are for and why they're safe to be public
# (they identify the project, they don't grant access - Firestore Security
# Rules do that).
#
# The filename matters, not just its presence: Vite only loads
# `.env.production` in "production" mode (plain `npm run build`, and
# GitHub Pages' deploy build). `npm run dev`, `npm run test:e2e`, and
# `npm run test:rules` all build/run in other modes on purpose, so they
# keep using src/cloudSync.ts's "demo-times-tables-quizzer" emulator
# default regardless of whether this file exists - a bare `.env` would
# instead apply to every mode, silently pointing local dev/test at your
# real project too. Don't rename this to plain `.env`.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
